// "Head Start": a swung hip-hop strut at 104, in G minor, forty-three bars, about a minute and
// forty seconds. Original music, written here, by Claude for Ryan. The brief: electronic, jazz
// and hip hop at once, in the vein of an anime's summer arc; spicy; it has to slap. Nothing of
// any recording or score is quoted.
//
// This is the fourth version, and the first built on a bed. The first three were a riff over
// nearly nothing, and a listener said of the third: "offbeat and weird and interesting, but it
// doesn't feel good". What changed is at the end of this comment.
//
// The concept. A cocky character's cue: someone who counts you down before he moves. Light,
// cocky, with one dark moment a phrase. A swung break at 104 (the off sixteenths fall 58% of
// the way between their eighths) under a riff you could clap, over chords that are always
// sounding. The piece never leaves G minor, so it can be cut anywhere.
//
// The bed, which has to feel good with the hook muted: bass drum on one and three, snare on two
// and four with ghost notes, hats; a sub and a round bass an octave over it; a soft piano
// holding each chord's third and seventh; a pad on B♭ and D, the two notes every chord of the
// piece shares. The chords are a cadence that comes round every two bars, a beat each:
// E♭maj9, D7♭9, G minor, and then the one.
//
// The hook is a countdown over that cadence. Two bars, said four times:
//
//   E♭maj9    D7♭9    Gm     A♭9♯11             (each number starts on a beat)
//   F F F F  F♯ F♯ F♯ · G G · ·  G♭––      ––––– · · · · · · · ·       four, three, two, ONE
//   F F F F  F♯ F♯ F♯ · G G · ·  G♭––      ––– G–– · · · · · ·         ... and it settles on G
//                                 Gm9
//   F F F F  F♯ F♯ F♯ · G G · ·  A'––      ––– G'––––––– ·             it comes home, and lets go
//   F F F F  F♯ F♯ F♯ · G G · ·  G♭––      ––– G · D D · · E♭E♭E♭ ·    ... two, three, and round again
//
// and, from bar 35, the form that ends it:
//
//   F F F F  F♯ F♯ F♯ · G G · ·  F♯''––    G''––––––                   four, three, two, one, ZERO
//
// A note is struck four times, a half-step higher three times, higher again twice, and each of
// the three is a chord tone: the ninth of E♭ major, the third of D7 (the leading note on its
// own chord), and G at home. All four voices of the piano's chords step up with it. Then the
// one, with the snare on four. Twice it drops a major seventh onto G♭, the seventh of a chord
// on A♭, a half-step over home: the piece's one dark thing. The first time it is cut off; the
// second it steps up to G. The third time is the release: the one steps up instead, a whole
// step after two half-steps, to A, a note the hook has not used, its highest, the ninth over
// G minor, held over the bar line; and it falls to G where the second saying's G♭ rose to it.
// The fourth drops again and counts back up, two on D and three on E♭, into the next four.
//
// At the end the one goes up the major seventh it used to fall, and steps up the half-step to
// G on the next first beat, where everyone strikes G minor: zero. It is the only place the
// tune sits on the tonic on a first beat, and that G is the piece's highest note. It lands
// three times, held longer each time: two beats (bar 36), three (bar 40), then to the end (42).
//
// The palette, by role, each role layered:
//   foundation    a short bass drum, a snare tuned to G, hats, a shaker, a ride at the end;
//                 the sub, and the round bass an octave up, so the line is there on a phone
//   held          the pad on B♭ and D; the soft piano's thirds and sevenths
//   moving        the keys' stutter; the shaker's sixteenths
//   lead          the keys' top line; from bar 29 a sung lead, with a pluck an octave over it
//   fill          the drums in the hook's rests; a pluck echoing "two, one"; two pairs of hands
//   and           a voice for the middle; a riser into each drop
//
// The form, with each part's energy out of ten:
//
// - bars 1-4, the count-in (3): the rhythm clapped over the pad; on the one the sub drops to
//   A♭ and slides home. Again with the keys on one note, F. Then two, three.
// - bars 5-12, said plainly (7): the keys in octaves over the bed.
// - bars 13-20, with its chords (8): the keys play the cadence; a shaker, sixteenths on the
//   hats, the pluck's echo. It settles, the drums say "two, one", and everything stops.
// - bars 21-28, the hands (3 to 6): one pair of hands claps the countdown over the soft piano,
//   which holds G minor while its lowest voice falls by half-steps. From bar 25 the second pair
//   joins half a bar behind, the same every bar, and a voice sings the countdown at a quarter
//   of its speed, sliding down the major seventh onto the one. Two, three.
// - bars 29-36, everything (10): the sung lead has the hook, the pluck its top octave, a ride.
//   The fourth time it lands: zero, for two beats, and two, three.
// - bars 37-43, the trade, and home (10): the one drops once more; the drums take most of a
//   bar, and everyone comes in early with five. Twice more the count lands, with every voice
//   and both pairs of hands striking it together: zero for three beats (bar 40), then held to
//   the end.
//
// An ear's notes, and what each changed.
// - On the first version (it hung on the one to the end): the build-up in the melody is really
//   nice, the escalating high notes, and so is holding off the full resolution; but it left the
//   listener craving it. The second added the landings on the high G and a resolved ending.
// - On the second: not only at the end; a melodic or harmonic release inside the main hook, like
//   one note in a pop chorus that is unexpected and satisfying (not that literally: ideas like
//   it). That chorus, read from a community transcription (Hooktheory's of Ariana Grande's
//   "positions"; none of it is used), says a pattern twice and then swerves onto a fresh note
//   that sits sweetly on a chord that has just arrived. The third version's third saying is
//   made on that idea.
// - On the third: the soft resolution chords are very nice; but it is offbeat and weird and
//   interesting and doesn't feel good, and tone, texture and layering are missing. Counted
//   against a piece the same listener praised, the third version struck 18% of its notes hard
//   (2% there), had a semitone sounding 46% of the time (10%), put 23% of its hook's notes on a
//   beat (41%), and its bass was almost all sub. So this version: the cadence the listener
//   liked is under every countdown; each number starts on a beat; no voicing has a semitone in
//   it; nothing is struck harder than forte; the harmony is always held (the cushion, the pad);
//   the bass has an audible octave; the lead is sung, not buzzed; a shaker, and echoes in the
//   rests. Gone: the chords slid in parallel, the sharp-eleventh slam with a second on top, the
//   growl, the canon that drifted an eighth a bar.
//
// No ear has heard this version. Counted by scripts/feel.py: no notes struck hard, a semitone
// sounding 4% of the time, a chord sounding 86% of it, 40% of the hook's notes on a beat, no
// flags. The mix: -10.1 LUFS, crest 11.6 dB, tilt -2.0 dB an octave, peak -1.0 dB, nothing
// clipped. What it wants that the engine lacks: a chorus on the pad and the piano, and a slow
// sweep on the pad's filter.
//
// What would need citing if this is kept (docs/citations.md is not touched here): the swing
// figure from Frane's study of drum breaks (Music Perception 34(3), 2017); the transcription
// the release was studied from (hooktheory.com/theorytab/view/ariana-grande/positions); for the
// rebuild, Reber, Schwarz and Winkielman on fluency and pleasure (PSPR 8(4), 2004), Witek et al.
// on syncopation and groove (PLoS ONE 9(4), 2014) and Lahdelma and Eerola on which chords are
// liked (i-Perception 7(3), 2016).

use engine::drum::{CLAP, Drum, HAT, KICK, OPEN_HAT, RIM, SNARE}
use engine::pattern::{Feel, Pattern, pattern, struck, swung, tacet}
use engine::perform::{Mark, Performance, Taste, bar, perform}
use engine::score::{Meter, Score, meter, score}
use engine::session::{Master, Session, Strip, session}
use engine::synth::{LEAD, PAD, PLUCK, Patch, SUB}
use engine::tine::{SUITCASE, Tine}
use engine::tone::Shape

pub const TITLE: Text = "Head Start"
pub const TEMPO: f32 = 104.0
pub const BARS: u32 = 43
const SWING: f32 = 0.58

fn four() -> Meter {
    meter(beats: 4, unit: 4)
}

// ---- the sounds -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// The bass drum: higher and shorter than the kit's, so it knocks above the bass and leaves the
/// lowest octave to it.
const THUD: Drum = Drum {
    tone_hz: 66.0,
    tone_t60: 0.26,
    sweep: 3.2,
    sweep_time: 0.012,
    drive: 2.8,
    click: 0.2,
    ..KICK,
}

/// The snare: its skin tuned to G, its wires brighter and a little longer.
const SMACK: Drum = Drum {
    tone_hz: 196.0,
    second_hz: 420.0,
    noise: 1.5,
    band_hz: 1900.0,
    top_hz: 8500.0,
    noise_t60: 0.24,
    click: 0.3,
    ..SNARE,
}

/// The hands that count: a drier clap, two bursts and a short tail.
const HANDS: Drum = Drum { band_hz: 1300.0, noise_t60: 0.14, bursts: 2, ..CLAP }

/// The second pair of hands: lower and a little looser, so the two can be told apart.
const OTHER_HANDS: Drum = Drum {
    band_hz: 950.0,
    noise_t60: 0.16,
    bursts: 2,
    burst_gap: 0.012,
    ..CLAP,
}

/// A shaker: a short breath of high noise, softer and duller when it is struck softly.
const SHAKER: Drum = Drum {
    noise: 1.0,
    band_hz: 7200.0,
    band_q: 1.1,
    cut_hz: 4500.0,
    noise_t60: 0.06,
    range_db: 18.0,
    soft_hz: 5000.0,
    ring_touch: 0.4,
}

/// A ride cymbal: the hi-hat's metal lower and wider, ringing most of a second.
const RIDE: Drum = Drum {
    metal_tune: 1.3,
    noise: 0.12,
    band_hz: 6800.0,
    band_q: 0.5,
    cut_hz: 3800.0,
    noise_t60: 0.8,
    ring_touch: 0.1,
    range_db: 18.0,
    ..HAT,
}

/// A crash cymbal: metal and noise together, wide open, two seconds long.
const CRASH: Drum = Drum {
    metal: 0.8,
    metal_tune: 1.15,
    noise: 0.9,
    band_hz: 6000.0,
    band_q: 0.4,
    cut_hz: 2600.0,
    noise_t60: 2.0,
    ring_touch: 0.0,
    ..HAT,
}

/// The bass's lowest layer: the sub, driven harder and ringing longer, so a held note is a drum
/// machine's long bass drum; it slides slowly enough between slurred notes for the slide to be
/// heard.
const DEEP: Patch = Patch {
    glide: 0.14,
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.004, decay: 2.6, sustain: 0.0, release: 0.06 },
    drive: 2.8,
    ..SUB,
}

/// The bass's second layer, an octave over the sub: round, a triangle and a sine with a little
/// sawtooth under a low filter, so the line is there on a speaker that can't play the sub.
const ROUND: Patch = Patch {
    saw: 0.2,
    triangle: 0.6,
    sine: 0.5,
    glide: 0.12,
    cutoff: 420.0,
    open: 1.4,
    q: 0.8,
    follow: 0.3,
    touch: 0.4,
    filter: Shape { attack: 0.004, decay: 0.25, sustain: 0.3, release: 0.1 },
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.005, decay: 0.9, sustain: 0.55, release: 0.08 },
    drive: 1.2,
    lean: 0.2,
    range_db: 10.0,
    voices: 1,
    level: 0.5,
}

/// The lead: a triangle over a sawtooth, sung more than buzzed, its filter opened by a hard key,
/// sliding between slurred notes, its vibrato late.
const WARM: Patch = Patch {
    saw: 0.35,
    triangle: 0.55,
    spread: 6.0,
    wide: 0.4,
    glide: 0.05,
    vibrato: 11.0,
    vibrato_hz: 5.4,
    vibrato_wake: 0.28,
    cutoff: 760.0,
    open: 2.6,
    q: 1.0,
    follow: 0.55,
    touch: 0.8,
    filter: Shape { attack: 0.006, decay: 0.3, sustain: 0.5, release: 0.2 },
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.006, decay: 0.5, sustain: 0.85, release: 0.12 },
    drive: 0.6,
    range_db: 12.0,
    voices: 1,
    level: 0.4,
}

/// The voice of the middle: the sung lead, slower between notes, so its fall of a seventh is a
/// slide.
const SUNG: Patch = Patch { glide: 0.14, ..LEAD }

/// The bed: the pad, a little darker, opening over a bar and quick to stop.
const BED: Patch = Patch {
    cutoff: 480.0,
    open: 1.6,
    q: 0.9,
    filter: Shape { attack: 2.0, decay: 3.0, sustain: 0.55, release: 0.3 },
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.6, decay: 1.0, sustain: 0.85, release: 0.25 },
    ..PAD,
}

/// A riser: noise and two sawtooths through a filter that takes two bars to open, climbing (its
/// notes are slurred, so it slides from each to the next).
const RISER: Patch = Patch {
    saw: 0.25,
    noise: 0.5,
    spread: 14.0,
    wide: 1.0,
    glide: 2.2,
    cutoff: 300.0,
    open: 5.0,
    q: 2.2,
    filter: Shape { attack: 3.8, decay: 1.0, sustain: 1.0, release: 0.05 },
    amp: Shape { attack: 3.6, decay: 1.0, sustain: 1.0, release: 0.04 },
    range_db: 6.0,
    voices: 1,
    level: 0.3,
}

/// The piano that says the hook: between the mellow one and the one that barks, with a little
/// more of the bell, played at a middling touch.
const BRIGHT: Tine = Tine {
    bell: 0.12,
    pole: 0.38,
    knock: 0.08,
    top_hz: 9000.0,
    tremolo: 0.4,
    ..SUITCASE,
}

// ---- the drums --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// The bars are named for what the hook does in them: `C` the countdown (its one on the fourth
// beat), `A1` the bar after it where the one hangs and is cut off (the drums answer), `A2` where
// it settles, `LA` the bar after the release, `T` the turn (two, three), `STOP` the bar
// everything stops in, `U` the countdown struck by everyone.

/// A drum's part: the bars' text.
fn drum(name: Text, lines: [Text]) -> Pattern {
    pattern(name, four(), lines)
}

fn silent(bars: u32) -> Pattern {
    tacet(four(), bars: bars)
}

const NOTHING: Text = ".... .... .... .... |"
/// One hit on the first beat: zero.
const HIT: Text = "X... .... .... .... |"

/// The countdown: four, three, two, one, each number starting on a beat.
const COUNT: Text = "xxxx xxx. xx.. X... |"
/// Five: five sixteenths from the off-beat of three, before the last countdowns.
const FIVE: Text = ".... .... ..xx xxx. |"

const KICK_C: Text = "x... ...x x... X... |"
const KICK_A1: Text = "x... ..x. x..x ..x. |"
const KICK_A2: Text = "x... ..x. ...x ..x. |"
/// The bar after the release, and the bars after zero: the beat, at home.
const KICK_HOME: Text = "x... ..x. x... ..x. |"
/// Two on the third beat and three on the fourth, after half a bar of the beat.
const KICK_T: Text = "x... ..x. xx.. xxx. |"
const KICK_STOP: Text = "x... ..x. ...X .... |"
/// The bar the drums have most of alone; everyone comes in early, with five.
const KICK_BREAK: Text = "x... ..x. ..X. .... |"
/// The countdown with everyone: the bass drum on each number.
const KICK_U: Text = "X... X... X... X... |"

fn kick() -> Pattern {
    let said = drum(
        "kick",
        [KICK_C, KICK_A1, KICK_C, KICK_A2, KICK_C, KICK_HOME, KICK_C, KICK_T],
    )
    let stopped = drum(
        "kick",
        [KICK_C, KICK_A1, KICK_C, KICK_A2, KICK_C, KICK_HOME, KICK_C, KICK_STOP],
    )
    // The middle's last four bars: the first beat of each and the one. Two, three is left to
    // the snare and the keys, so the lows are gone for the half bar before the drop.
    let half = drum(
        "kick",
        ["x... .... .... .... | x... .... ..x. .... | x... .... .... X... |", NOTHING],
    )
    silent(4)
        .then(said.clone())
        .then(stopped)
        .then(silent(4))
        .then(half)
        .then(said)
        .then(drum("kick", [KICK_C, KICK_BREAK, KICK_U, KICK_HOME, KICK_U, HIT]))
        .then(silent(1))
}

/// Two, three on the snare alone, before a drop.
const SNARE_UP: Text = ".... .... oo.. xxX. |"
const SNARE_C: Text = "...o X... .o.. X... |"
const SNARE_A1: Text = ".... X..o .o.. X..o |"
const SNARE_A2: Text = ".... X..o .o.. X.ox |"
const SNARE_LA: Text = ".... X... .o.. X..o |"
const SNARE_T: Text = ".... X... xx.. xxX. |"
/// "Two, one", and nothing after it.
const SNARE_STOP: Text = ".... X... xx.X .... |"
/// The drums' bar: the backbeat on four comes an eighth early, and then five, getting louder.
const SNARE_BREAK: Text = ".... X.o. o.Xo xxX. |"
const SNARE_U: Text = "Xxxx Xxx. Xx.. X... |"

fn snare() -> Pattern {
    let said = drum(
        "snare",
        [SNARE_C, SNARE_A1, SNARE_C, SNARE_A2, SNARE_C, SNARE_LA, SNARE_C, SNARE_T],
    )
    let stopped = drum(
        "snare",
        [SNARE_C, SNARE_A1, SNARE_C, SNARE_A2, SNARE_C, SNARE_LA, SNARE_C, SNARE_STOP],
    )
    silent(3)
        .then(drum("snare", [SNARE_UP]))
        .then(said.clone())
        .then(stopped)
        .then(silent(6))
        .then(drum("snare", [".... .... .... X... |", SNARE_UP]))
        .then(said)
        .then(drum("snare", [SNARE_C, SNARE_BREAK, SNARE_U, SNARE_A1, SNARE_U, HIT]))
        .then(silent(1))
}

/// The first pair of hands: the countdown, in the count-in, through the middle (where the last
/// bar stops for two, three), and with everyone in bars 39 and 41, each followed by one clap on
/// the next first beat: zero.
fn hands() -> Pattern {
    let count = drum("hands", [COUNT])
    count
        .clone()
        .then(silent(1))
        .then(count.clone())
        .then(silent(17))
        .then(count.times(7))
        .then(drum("hands", ["xxxx xxx. .... .... |"]))
        .then(silent(9))
        .then(drum("hands", [FIVE, COUNT, HIT, COUNT, HIT]))
        .then(silent(1))
}

/// The second pair: with the first in the count-in and at the end. In the middle it waits four
/// bars, then claps the countdown half a bar behind the first pair, the same every bar: a round
/// for two.
fn other_hands() -> Pattern {
    let count = drum("other hands", [COUNT])
    let behind = drum("other hands", ["xx.. X... xxxx xxx. |"])
    count
        .clone()
        .then(silent(1))
        .then(count.clone())
        .then(silent(21))
        .then(behind.times(3))
        .then(drum("other hands", ["xx.. X... .... .... |"]))
        .then(silent(9))
        .then(drum("other hands", [FIVE, COUNT, HIT, COUNT, HIT]))
        .then(silent(1))
}

const HAT_C: Text = "X.x. X.xo X.x. .... |"
const HAT_A1: Text = "X.x. X.x. X.xo X.x. |"
const HAT_A2: Text = "X.x. X.xo X.x. X.x. |"
const HAT_T: Text = "X.x. X.x. .... .... |"
const HAT_C16: Text = "X.xo X.xo X.x. .... |"
const HAT_A16: Text = "X.xo X.xo X.xo X.x. |"
const HAT_U: Text = "Xxxx Xxx. Xx.. .... |"

fn hat() -> Pattern {
    let eighths = drum("hat", [HAT_C, HAT_A1, HAT_C, HAT_A2, HAT_C, HAT_A1, HAT_C, HAT_T])
    let sixteenths = drum(
        "hat",
        [HAT_C16, HAT_A16, HAT_C16, HAT_A16, HAT_C16, HAT_A16, HAT_C16, HAT_T],
    )
    silent(2)
        .then(drum("hat", ["o.o. o.o. o.o. o.o. | o.o. o.o. .... .... |"]))
        .then(eighths)
        .then(sixteenths.clone())
        .then(silent(8))
        .then(sixteenths)
        .then(drum("hat", [HAT_C16, "X.x. X.x. X.x. .... |", HAT_U, HAT_A16, HAT_U]))
        .then(silent(2))
}

/// The shaker: sixteenths, the off ones a little harder, under the second statement and from
/// bar 29; it stops before each one, with the hats.
fn shaker() -> Pattern {
    let c: Text = "oxox oxox ox.. .... |"
    let a: Text = "oxox oxox oxox oxox |"
    let t: Text = "oxox oxox .... .... |"
    let round = drum("shaker", [c, a, c, a, c, a, c, t])
    silent(12)
        .then(round.clone())
        .then(silent(8))
        .then(round)
        .then(drum("shaker", [c, c, NOTHING, a]))
        .then(silent(3))
}

/// The open hat rings on the one, and the next bar's first closed hat stops it.
fn open_hat() -> Pattern {
    let one: Text = ".... .... .... X... |"
    let round = drum("open hat", [one, NOTHING, one, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, one, NOTHING])
    silent(4)
        .then(round.times(2))
        .then(silent(8))
        .then(round)
        .then(drum("open hat", [one, NOTHING, one, NOTHING, one]))
        .then(silent(2))
}

fn ride() -> Pattern {
    let c: Text = "X.x. X.x. X.x. .... |"
    let a: Text = "X.x. X.x. X.x. X.x. |"
    silent(28)
        .then(drum("ride", [c, a, c, a, c, a, c, "X.x. X.x. .... .... |", c]))
        .then(silent(2))
        .then(drum("ride", [a]))
        .then(silent(3))
}

/// A crash where a part starts (bars 5, 13, 29), on the one that is released (bars 9, 17, 33)
/// and the middle's (27), and on every zero: the first beats of bars 36, 40 and 42.
fn crash() -> Pattern {
    let first = drum("crash", ["X... .... .... ...."])
    let fourth = drum("crash", [".... .... .... X..."])
    let soft_fourth = drum("crash", [".... .... .... x..."])
    silent(4)
        .then(first.clone())
        .then(silent(3))
        .then(soft_fourth.clone())
        .then(silent(3))
        .then(first.clone())
        .then(silent(3))
        .then(soft_fourth.clone())
        .then(silent(9))
        .then(soft_fourth)
        .then(silent(1))
        .then(first.clone())
        .then(silent(3))
        .then(fourth)
        .then(silent(2))
        .then(first.clone())
        .then(silent(3))
        .then(first.clone())
        .then(silent(1))
        .then(first)
        .then(silent(1))
}

/// A rim: the backbeat's place in the count-in, and the third beat in the middle's half time.
fn rim() -> Pattern {
    silent(2)
        .then(drum("rim", [".... x... .... ...."]))
        .then(silent(21))
        .then(drum("rim", [".... .... x... ...."]).times(2))
        .then(silent(17))
}

// ---- the parts written as notes ---------------------------------------------------------------

fn part(name: Text, lines: [Text]) -> Score {
    score(TITLE, four()).voice(name, lines)
}

/// `bars` bars of rest for the part `name`.
fn rests(name: Text, bars: u32) -> Score {
    var s = part(name, ["r/1 |"])
    for _ in 1..bars {
        s = take s.then(part(name, ["r/1 |"]))
    }
    s
}

const REST: Text = "r/1 |"

// The bass, in two layers that play the same line an octave apart: the sub (`BASS_`) and the
// round one over it (`ROUND_`). A countdown bar is `_COUNT` (E♭, D and G under four, three and
// two: the sixth, the fifth and home) and then the one: `_ONE` (A♭, tied over the bar line),
// `_ONE_SLIDES` (the same, slurred on, so it slides down to the next bar's G), `_SWEET` (G: the
// release) or `_LANDS` (A♭ for a beat, so G is struck on the next first beat). The bar after is
// `_HANG` (A♭ held and cut off), `_SETTLE` (the slide to G), `_HOME` (G held), `_UP` (the slide,
// then two, three on D) or `_STOP`; each but the last two ends on D, a half-step under the next
// bar's E♭.
const BASS_COUNT: Text = "eb2/4 !f d2/8. r/16 g1/8 r/8"
const BASS_ONE: Text = "ab1/4~ |"
const BASS_ONE_SLIDES: Text = "ab1/4 ( ~ |"
const BASS_SWEET: Text = "g1/4~ |"
const BASS_LANDS: Text = "ab1/4 |"
const BASS_HANG: Text = "ab1/2 r/4 r/8 d2/8 |"
const BASS_SETTLE: Text = "ab1/4. g1/4 ) r/4 d2/8 |"
const BASS_HOME: Text = "g1/2 r/4 r/8 d2/8 |"
const BASS_UP: Text = "ab1/4. g1/8 ) d2/16 d2 r/8 d2/16 d2 d2 r/16 |"
const BASS_STOP: Text = "ab1/4. g1/4 ) r/4. |"
/// Zero for two beats, then two, three.
const BASS_ZERO_UP: Text = "g1/2 !ff d2/16 !f d2 r/8 d2/16 d2 d2 r/16 |"
/// Bar 38: the one cut off, then D held under five.
const BASS_FIVE: Text = "ab1/2 r/8 d2/4~ d2/16 r/16 |"

fn bass() -> Score {
    let count_in = part(
        "bass",
        ["r/2. ab1/4 !mf ( ~ | ab1/2 g1/2 ) | r/2. ab1/4 ( ~ | ab1/4. g1/8 ) r/2 |"],
    )
    let said = part(
        "bass",
        [
            BASS_COUNT,
            BASS_ONE,
            BASS_HANG,
            BASS_COUNT,
            BASS_ONE_SLIDES,
            BASS_SETTLE,
            BASS_COUNT,
            BASS_SWEET,
            BASS_HOME,
            BASS_COUNT,
            BASS_ONE_SLIDES,
            BASS_UP,
        ],
    )
    let stopped = part(
        "bass",
        [
            BASS_COUNT,
            BASS_ONE,
            BASS_HANG,
            BASS_COUNT,
            BASS_ONE_SLIDES,
            BASS_SETTLE,
            BASS_COUNT,
            BASS_SWEET,
            BASS_HOME,
            BASS_COUNT,
            BASS_ONE_SLIDES,
            BASS_STOP,
        ],
    )
    // The middle: E♭ sliding to D, G, and the one, which stops before two, three.
    let half = part("bass", ["eb2/1 !mf ( | d2/1 ) | g1/2. !f ab1/4~ |", "ab1/2 r/2 |"])
    // Bars 29-36: as it was said, but the last one lands.
    let lands = part(
        "bass",
        [
            BASS_COUNT,
            BASS_ONE,
            BASS_HANG,
            BASS_COUNT,
            BASS_ONE_SLIDES,
            BASS_SETTLE,
            BASS_COUNT,
            BASS_SWEET,
            BASS_HOME,
            BASS_COUNT,
            BASS_LANDS,
            BASS_ZERO_UP,
        ],
    )
    // Bars 37-43: the one hangs once more; five; then twice the count lands on G, the second
    // time for good.
    let trade = part(
        "bass",
        [
            BASS_COUNT,
            BASS_ONE,
            BASS_FIVE,
            BASS_COUNT,
            BASS_LANDS,
            "g1/2. !ff r/8 d2/8 !f |",
            BASS_COUNT,
            BASS_LANDS,
            "g1/1~ !ff | g1/1 |",
        ],
    )
    (take count_in)
        .then(said)
        .then(stopped)
        .then(rests("bass", bars: 4))
        .then(half)
        .then(lands)
        .then(trade)
}

const ROUND_COUNT: Text = "eb3/4 !mf d3/8. r/16 g2/8 r/8"
const ROUND_ONE: Text = "ab2/4~ |"
const ROUND_ONE_SLIDES: Text = "ab2/4 ( ~ |"
const ROUND_SWEET: Text = "g2/4~ |"
const ROUND_LANDS: Text = "ab2/4 |"
const ROUND_HANG: Text = "ab2/2 r/4 r/8 d3/8 |"
const ROUND_SETTLE: Text = "ab2/4. g2/4 ) r/4 d3/8 |"
const ROUND_HOME: Text = "g2/2 r/4 r/8 d3/8 |"
const ROUND_UP: Text = "ab2/4. g2/8 ) d3/16 d3 r/8 d3/16 d3 d3 r/16 |"
const ROUND_STOP: Text = "ab2/4. g2/4 ) r/4. |"
const ROUND_ZERO_UP: Text = "g2/2 !f d3/16 !mf d3 r/8 d3/16 d3 d3 r/16 |"
const ROUND_FIVE: Text = "ab2/2 r/8 d3/16 d3 d3 d3 d3 r/16 |"

/// The bass's round layer: the sub's line an octave up, from the first statement on.
fn round() -> Score {
    let said = part(
        "round",
        [
            ROUND_COUNT,
            ROUND_ONE,
            ROUND_HANG,
            ROUND_COUNT,
            ROUND_ONE_SLIDES,
            ROUND_SETTLE,
            ROUND_COUNT,
            ROUND_SWEET,
            ROUND_HOME,
            ROUND_COUNT,
            ROUND_ONE_SLIDES,
            ROUND_UP,
        ],
    )
    let stopped = part(
        "round",
        [
            ROUND_COUNT,
            ROUND_ONE,
            ROUND_HANG,
            ROUND_COUNT,
            ROUND_ONE_SLIDES,
            ROUND_SETTLE,
            ROUND_COUNT,
            ROUND_SWEET,
            ROUND_HOME,
            ROUND_COUNT,
            ROUND_ONE_SLIDES,
            ROUND_STOP,
        ],
    )
    let half = part("round", ["eb3/1 !mp ( | d3/1 ) | g2/2. !mf ab2/4~ |", "ab2/2 r/2 |"])
    let lands = part(
        "round",
        [
            ROUND_COUNT,
            ROUND_ONE,
            ROUND_HANG,
            ROUND_COUNT,
            ROUND_ONE_SLIDES,
            ROUND_SETTLE,
            ROUND_COUNT,
            ROUND_SWEET,
            ROUND_HOME,
            ROUND_COUNT,
            ROUND_LANDS,
            ROUND_ZERO_UP,
        ],
    )
    let trade = part(
        "round",
        [
            ROUND_COUNT,
            ROUND_ONE,
            ROUND_FIVE,
            ROUND_COUNT,
            ROUND_LANDS,
            "g2/2. !f r/8 d3/8 !mf |",
            ROUND_COUNT,
            ROUND_LANDS,
            "g2/1~ !f | g2/1 |",
        ],
    )
    rests("round", bars: 4)
        .then(said)
        .then(stopped)
        .then(rests("round", bars: 4))
        .then(half)
        .then(lands)
        .then(trade)
}

// The hook on the keys. A countdown bar is the stutter and then the one. `STUTTER_8` is the
// stutter in octaves; `STUTTER_9` puts each number on its chord, all four voices stepping up
// together: E♭maj9 (F its ninth), D7 with a flat ninth (F♯ its third), G minor (G). `ONE` is
// A♭ with its ninth and sharp eleventh, G♭ on top and at the bottom, tied over the bar line;
// `SWEET_ONE` is the one that steps up: A on top of G minor's ninth chord. The bar after: `HANG`
// (held two beats and cut off), `SETTLE` (stepping up to G minor, G on top), `SWEET_BAR` (the A
// falls to G, on a plain G minor chord), `TURN_8` (settling, then two on D and three on E♭).
// No voicing has a semitone in it.
const STUTTER_8: Text = "<f4 f5>/16 !mf !accent <f4 f5> <f4 f5> <f4 f5> <f#4 f#5>/16 !accent <f#4 f#5> <f#4 f#5> r/16 <g4 g5>/16 !accent <g4 g5> r/8"
const STUTTER_9: Text = "<g4 bb4 d5 f5>/16 !mf !accent <g4 bb4 d5 f5> <g4 bb4 d5 f5> <g4 bb4 d5 f5> <a4 c5 eb5 f#5>/16 !accent <a4 c5 eb5 f#5> <a4 c5 eb5 f#5> r/16 <g4 bb4 d5 g5>/16 !accent <g4 bb4 d5 g5> r/8"
const ONE: Text = "<gb3 bb3 c4 d4 gb4>/4~ !f !tenuto |"
const SWEET_ONE: Text = "<bb3 d4 f4 a4 d5 a5>/4~ !mf !tenuto |"
const HANG: Text = "<gb3 bb3 c4 d4 gb4>/2 r/2 |"
const SETTLE: Text = "<gb3 bb3 c4 d4 gb4>/4. <g3 bb3 d4 g4>/4 !mf !tenuto r/4. |"
const SWEET_BAR: Text = "<bb3 d4 f4 a4 d5 a5>/4. <g4 bb4 d5 g5>/2 !mf !tenuto r/8 |"
const TURN_8: Text = "<gb3 bb3 c4 d4 gb4>/4. <g3 bb3 d4 g4>/8 !mf <d4 d5>/16 <d4 d5> r/8 <eb4 eb5>/16 <eb4 eb5> <eb4 eb5> r/16 |"
/// Two, three alone, in the second half of a bar: in octaves (bar 4), and on D7 (bar 28).
const UP_8: Text = "r/2 <d4 d5>/16 !mp <d4 d5> r/8 <eb4 eb5>/16 <eb4 eb5> <eb4 eb5> r/16 |"
const UP_9: Text = "r/2 <f#4 a4 c5 d5>/16 !mf <f#4 a4 c5 d5> r/8 <f#4 a4 c5 eb5>/16 <f#4 a4 c5 eb5> <f#4 a4 c5 eb5> r/16 |"
/// Bar 38: the one cut off, and then five on D7's flat ninth.
const HANG_FIVE: Text = "<gb3 bb3 c4 d4 gb4>/2 r/8 <f#4 a4 c5 eb5>/16 !mf <f#4 a4 c5 eb5> <f#4 a4 c5 eb5> <f#4 a4 c5 eb5> <f#4 a4 c5 eb5> r/16 |"
/// The one that lands: A♭13 with its seventh, G♭, on top an octave higher, for one beat; then
/// zero, G minor with its ninth and G on top, struck on the first beat: `HOME_TURN` holds it two
/// beats and goes on to two, three; `HOME` holds it three; `HOME_LAST` two bars.
const ONE_UP: Text = "<gb3 c4 f4 bb4 gb5>/4 !f !tenuto |"
const HOME_TURN: Text = "<g3 bb3 d4 a4 d5 g5>/2 !f !tenuto <f#4 a4 c5 d5>/16 !mf <f#4 a4 c5 d5> r/8 <f#4 a4 c5 eb5>/16 <f#4 a4 c5 eb5> <f#4 a4 c5 eb5> r/16 |"
const HOME: Text = "<g3 bb3 d4 a4 d5 g5>/2. !f !tenuto r/4 |"
const HOME_LAST: Text = "<g3 bb3 d4 a4 d5 g5>/1~ !f !tenuto | <g3 bb3 d4 a4 d5 g5>/1 |"

/// The keys: the piano at a middling touch, without its pedal. The countdown's rhythm on F alone
/// (bar 3); the hook in octaves (5-12); with its chords (13-20, ending settled); two, three out
/// of the middle (28); the chords again under the lead (29-36), and to the end.
fn keys() -> Score {
    let count_in = part(
        "keys",
        ["r/1 | r/1 |", "f5/16 !mp f5 f5 f5 f5/16 f5 f5 r/16 f5/16 f5 r/8 f5/4 |", UP_8],
    )
    let plain = part(
        "keys",
        [
            STUTTER_8,
            ONE,
            HANG,
            STUTTER_8,
            ONE,
            SETTLE,
            STUTTER_8,
            SWEET_ONE,
            SWEET_BAR,
            STUTTER_8,
            ONE,
            TURN_8,
        ],
    )
    let chords = part(
        "keys",
        [
            STUTTER_9,
            ONE,
            HANG,
            STUTTER_9,
            ONE,
            SETTLE,
            STUTTER_9,
            SWEET_ONE,
            SWEET_BAR,
            STUTTER_9,
            ONE,
            SETTLE,
        ],
    )
    let last = part(
        "keys",
        [
            STUTTER_9,
            ONE,
            HANG,
            STUTTER_9,
            ONE,
            SETTLE,
            STUTTER_9,
            SWEET_ONE,
            SWEET_BAR,
            STUTTER_9,
            ONE_UP,
            HOME_TURN,
        ],
    )
    let trade = part(
        "keys",
        [STUTTER_9, ONE, HANG_FIVE, STUTTER_9, ONE_UP, HOME, STUTTER_9, ONE_UP, HOME_LAST],
    )
    (take count_in)
        .then(plain)
        .then(chords)
        .then(rests("keys", bars: 7))
        .then(part("keys", [UP_9]))
        .then(last)
        .then(trade)
}

/// The cushion under a countdown bar: each number's chord as its third and seventh, held a
/// whole beat under the stutter, the two voices falling by half-steps (G, F♯, F over D, C, B♭);
/// the one is left to the others.
const CUSHION: Text = "<g3 d4>/4 !mp !tenuto <f#3 c4>/4 !tenuto <f3 bb3>/4 !tenuto r/4 |"

/// The soft keys: the same piano played softly and held. Under the statements, the cushion. In
/// the middle, each chord its whole bar: G minor with its ninth while the lowest voice falls by
/// half-steps (G, F♯, F, E), then E♭maj9, D7♭13, G minor and the one, A♭13♯11.
fn soft_keys() -> Score {
    let under = || -> Score {
        part("soft keys", [CUSHION, REST, CUSHION, REST, CUSHION, REST, CUSHION, REST])
    }
    let middle = part(
        "soft keys",
        [
            "<g3 bb3 d4 a4>/1 !p !tenuto | <f#3 bb3 d4 a4>/1 !tenuto |",
            "<f3 bb3 d4 a4>/1 !tenuto | <e3 bb3 d4 a4>/1 !tenuto |",
            "<eb3 g3 bb3 d4 f4>/1 !mp !tenuto | <d3 f#3 c4 bb4>/1 !tenuto |",
            "<g3 bb3 d4 f4 a4>/2. !tenuto <gb3 bb3 c4 d4 f4>/4~ !mf !tenuto |",
            "<gb3 bb3 c4 d4 f4>/2 r/2 |",
        ],
    )
    rests("soft keys", bars: 4)
        .then(under())
        .then(under())
        .then(middle)
        .then(under())
        .then(part("soft keys", [CUSHION, REST, CUSHION, REST, CUSHION, REST, REST]))
}

/// Four bars of the bed, B♭ and D, a third: the two notes every chord of the piece holds
/// (G minor's third and fifth, E♭ major's fifth and seventh, D7's flat thirteenth and root,
/// A♭13's ninth and sharp eleventh). `BED_STOPS` lets go halfway through its last bar, and
/// `BED_BUILDS` a beat before its end.
const BED_4: Text = "<bb3 d4>/1~ !mp | <bb3 d4>/1~ | <bb3 d4>/1~ | <bb3 d4>/1 |"
const BED_STOPS: Text = "<bb3 d4>/1~ !mp | <bb3 d4>/1~ | <bb3 d4>/1~ | <bb3 d4>/2 r/2 |"
const BED_BUILDS: Text = "<bb3 d4>/1~ !mp | <bb3 d4>/1~ | <bb3 d4>/1~ | <bb3 d4>/2. r/4 |"

/// The bed: a pad on that third, from the first bar to the last.
fn bed() -> Score {
    part("bed", [BED_4, BED_4, BED_4, BED_4, BED_STOPS, BED_4, BED_BUILDS, BED_4, BED_4, BED_4])
        .then(part("bed", ["<bb3 d4>/1~ !mp | <bb3 d4>/1~ | <bb3 d4>/1 |"]))
}

/// The pluck's echo, where the hook rests: "two, one" on D, on the beats the hook's two and one
/// fell on a bar before; the second time the one falls to A.
const ECHO: Text = "r/2 d6/16 !mp d6 r/8 d6/4 |"
const ECHO_FALLS: Text = "r/2 d6/16 !mp d6 r/8 a5/4 |"
/// The stutter an octave over the lead (the one is left to the others).
const PLUCK_STUTTER: Text = "f6/16 !mp f6 f6 f6 f#6/16 f#6 f#6 r/16 g6/16 g6 r/8 r/4 |"
/// The stutter and the one that steps up, with the lead (bar 33).
const PLUCK_SWEET: Text = "f6/16 !mp f6 f6 f6 f#6/16 f#6 f#6 r/16 g6/16 g6 r/8 a6/4 |"
/// The stutter and the one that lands, with the lead; and zero, then two, three.
const PLUCK_LANDS: Text = "f6/16 !mp f6 f6 f6 f#6/16 f#6 f#6 r/16 g6/16 g6 r/8 f#6/4 |"
const PLUCK_ZERO_UP: Text = "g6/4 !mf r/4 d6/16 !mp d6 r/8 eb6/16 eb6 eb6 r/16 |"

/// The pluck: the echo in the first two statements' rests; the hook's top octave and the echo
/// from bar 29.
fn pluck() -> Score {
    rests("pluck", bars: 4)
        .then(part("pluck", [REST, REST, REST, ECHO, REST, ECHO_FALLS, REST, REST]))
        .then(part("pluck", [REST, ECHO, REST, ECHO_FALLS, REST, ECHO, REST, REST]))
        .then(rests("pluck", bars: 8))
        .then(
            part(
                "pluck",
                [
                    PLUCK_STUTTER,
                    ECHO,
                    PLUCK_STUTTER,
                    ECHO_FALLS,
                    PLUCK_SWEET,
                    ECHO,
                    PLUCK_LANDS,
                    PLUCK_ZERO_UP,
                ],
            ),
        )
        .then(
            part(
                "pluck",
                [
                    PLUCK_STUTTER,
                    "r/2 r/8 eb6/16 !mp eb6 eb6 eb6 eb6 r/16 |",
                    PLUCK_LANDS,
                    "g6/4 !mf r/4 d6/16 !mp d6 r/8 d6/4 |",
                    PLUCK_LANDS,
                    "<g5 d6 g6>/2 !mf r/2 |",
                    REST,
                ],
            ),
        )
}

/// The voice of the middle (bars 25-28): the countdown at a quarter of its speed. F for four
/// beats, F♯ for three, G for two, then a slide down the major seventh onto the one, on the
/// fourth beat, held over the bar line.
fn voice() -> Score {
    rests("voice", bars: 24)
        .then(part("voice", ["f5/1 !mf | r/4 f#5/2. | r/4 g5/2 ( gb4/4~ | gb4/2 ) r/2 |"]))
        .then(rests("voice", bars: 15))
}

// The lead's bars, as the keys' are named.
const LEAD_STUTTER: Text = "f5/16 !mf !accent f5 f5 f5 f#5/16 !accent f#5 f#5 r/16 g5/16 !accent g5 r/8"
const LEAD_ONE: Text = "gb4/4~ !f |"
const LEAD_ONE_SLIDES: Text = "gb4/4 !f ( ~ |"
/// The third saying's one: it steps up to A, the ninth of G minor, held over the bar line, and
/// slides down to G.
const LEAD_SWEET: Text = "a5/4 !f ( ~ |"
/// The one that lands: up a major seventh, the drop turned over, and slurred on, so it slides
/// up the half-step to G on the next first beat. That G is the piece's highest note.
const LEAD_LANDS: Text = "f#6/4 !f ( |"
/// Zero for two beats, then two, three.
const LEAD_ZERO_UP: Text = "g6/2 !tenuto ) d5/16 !mf d5 r/8 eb5/16 eb5 eb5 r/16 |"
const LEAD_HANG: Text = "gb4/2 r/2 |"
const LEAD_SETTLE: Text = "gb4/4. g4/4 ) r/4. |"
const LEAD_SWEET_BAR: Text = "a5/4. g5/2 !tenuto ) r/8 |"

/// The lead (bars 29-42): the hook, sliding where it settles. The third time its one steps up
/// to the ninth and falls to G; the fourth it goes up the major seventh and lands on the high
/// G, held two beats (bar 36); after the drums' bar it lands twice more, held three beats (bar
/// 40) and then to the end (bar 42).
fn lead() -> Score {
    let said = part(
        "lead",
        [
            LEAD_STUTTER,
            LEAD_ONE,
            LEAD_HANG,
            LEAD_STUTTER,
            LEAD_ONE_SLIDES,
            LEAD_SETTLE,
            LEAD_STUTTER,
            LEAD_SWEET,
            LEAD_SWEET_BAR,
            LEAD_STUTTER,
            LEAD_LANDS,
            LEAD_ZERO_UP,
        ],
    )
    let trade = part(
        "lead",
        [
            LEAD_STUTTER,
            LEAD_ONE,
            "gb4/2 r/8 eb5/16 !mf eb5 eb5 eb5 eb5 r/16 |",
            LEAD_STUTTER,
            LEAD_LANDS,
            "g6/2. !tenuto ) r/4 |",
            LEAD_STUTTER,
            LEAD_LANDS,
            "g6/1 !tenuto ~ | g6/2 ) r/2 |",
        ],
    )
    rests("lead", bars: 28).then(said).then(trade)
}

/// The riser: two bars up into each drop, stopping a beat early.
fn riser() -> Score {
    let up = || -> Score { part("riser", ["c3/4 !mf ( c5/2. | c6/2. ) r/4 |"]) }
    rests("riser", bars: 2)
        .then(up())
        .then(rests("riser", bars: 22))
        .then(up())
        .then(rests("riser", bars: 15))
}

/// A score as a player with `taste` plays it, sitting in time as `feel` says.
fn played(s: Score, taste: Taste, feel: Feel) -> Performance {
    swung(perform(s, taste, [Mark::Hold { at: bar(1), by: 1.0 }; 0]), feel)
}

// ---- the session ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// The whole track, ready to play.
pub fn build() -> Session {
    var s = session(
        TEMPO,
        Master {
            gain: 4.0,
            glue_db: -16.0,
            glue: 0.35,
            makeup: 6.0,
            warmth: 1.0,
            ceiling: -1.0,
            room_time: 1.2,
            room_size: 1.4,
            room_db: -4.0,
            echo_beats: 0.75,
            echo_again: 0.4,
            echo_db: -5.0,
            duck_time: 0.13,
        },
    )
    // The drums: the bass drum on the grid, the snare behind it, the hats and the shaker ahead.
    s.drum(
        "kick",
        THUD,
        struck(kick(), TEMPO, Feel { swing: SWING, loose: 0.001, uneven: 0.03, seed: 1 }, key: 36),
        Strip { gain: -1.0, room: 0.03 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "snare",
        SMACK,
        struck(
            snare(),
            TEMPO,
            Feel { swing: SWING, late: 0.008, loose: 0.002, uneven: 0.08, seed: 2 },
            key: 38,
        ),
        Strip { gain: -4.5, low_cut: 110.0, drive: 1.4, room: 0.22 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "hands",
        HANDS,
        struck(hands(), TEMPO, Feel { swing: SWING, loose: 0.002, uneven: 0.1, seed: 14 }, key: 39),
        Strip { gain: -4.0, pan: -0.55, low_cut: 300.0, room: 0.3 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "other hands",
        OTHER_HANDS,
        struck(
            other_hands(),
            TEMPO,
            Feel { swing: SWING, loose: 0.002, uneven: 0.1, seed: 15 },
            key: 40,
        ),
        Strip { gain: -4.0, pan: 0.55, low_cut: 300.0, room: 0.3 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "hat",
        HAT,
        struck(
            hat(),
            TEMPO,
            Feel { swing: SWING, late: -0.004, loose: 0.002, uneven: 0.14, seed: 4 },
            key: 42,
        ),
        Strip { gain: -8.0, pan: 0.35, room: 0.06 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "shaker",
        SHAKER,
        struck(
            shaker(),
            TEMPO,
            Feel { swing: SWING, late: -0.003, loose: 0.003, uneven: 0.18, seed: 16 },
